smentlcd
========

A small daemon that controls SpaceMouse Enterprise LCD.

Motivation
==========

The vendor Linux driver for the SpaceMouse Enterprise is effectively
abandonware. On Linux, Blender relies on libspnav instead, which is backed by
the open-source spacenavd daemon.

spacenavd handles input well enough, but it completely ignores the LCD. Without
control over the display, the screen is just dead weight stuck showing the
default vendor logo.

Reading spacenavd's source shows that it never claims the LCD USB interface.
That leaves the door open: smentlcd uses libusb to claim only the LCD interface
and drive it directly, allowing arbitrary static images and GIFs to be rendered
on the display. It doesn't touch input handling and coexists cleanly alongside
spacenavd.

Platform Support
================

Developed and tested on Ubuntu 26.04 for personal use. Linux is the only
supported target. Porting to FreeBSD should be trivial given libusb, though it's
currently untested.

macOS support was originally planned -- which is why parts of the codebase (such
as the IPC layer) are more abstracted than a Linux-only daemon strictly needs.
That effort was dropped. On macOS, Blender relies on the official vendor driver,
and once that driver is running, the OS refuses to let libusb claim the required
USB interface. Under the current architecture, coexistence is simply unsolvable.
I have zero interest in fighting Apple's USB stack or rewriting the design
around it, and no other platforms are planned.

Documentation
=============

Full documentation lives in the Documentation directory (reStructuredText) and
is rendered online at:

	https://docs.barroit.sh/smentlcd

Entry points:

	Documentation/user-manual/	installation and usage
	Documentation/build-system/	build system
	Documentation/program/		program and command architecture
	Documentation/core-api/		core utility APIs
	Documentation/smentlcd-api/	smentlcd-specific APIs
	Documentation/test/		test suite
